"guide.build.body" = "The source package includes a pinned-engine bootstrap, a universal macOS app build script, tests and signing/notarization instructions. Developer ID signing and notarization require your own Apple Developer credentials.";
"guide.build.title" = "Built to be yours";
"guide.formats.body" = "Create 7z, ZIP, TAR, TAR.GZ, TAR.BZ2, TAR.XZ and single-file GZIP, BZIP2 or XZ. Read RAR/RAR5 and many other formats through 7-Zip and libarchive. Format variants and encrypted containers may have limitations; no app can promise every possible archive.";
"guide.formats.title" = "Read many. Write deliberately.";
"guide.parts.body" = "Set a part size such as 100 MiB when creating 7z, ZIP or RAR. Results are saved atomically in a .parts folder. Open any numbered part to locate the first volume. Missing parts must be restored before extraction. Split ZIP created by 7-Zip uses .zip.001, not the traditional .z01 naming.";
"guide.parts.title" = "Keep every part together";
"guide.password.body" = "Use AES-256 in 7z or ZIP for encryption. File-name encryption is available for 7z and licensed RAR, not ZIP. Passwords travel through standard input, not process arguments. Closing an archive clears its retained password; finishing a task clears that task’s secret.";
"guide.password.title" = "Protect the archive";
"guide.rar.body" = "Browse, test and extract RAR/RAR5 directly. To create RAR, open the download for your Mac architecture in Settings → Engines, import the original downloaded .tar.gz, then import your purchased rarreg.key. No manual installation or terminal setup is needed. After registration is confirmed, RAR5, solid compression, encryption and volumes are supported. Repair, REV and SFX creation are not provided.";
"guide.rar.title" = "RAR compatibility";
"guide.safety.body" = "Arcora processes files in a private temporary workspace, checks the result and commits to a new destination. Unsafe paths, links, devices and conflicting entry names are rejected. This conservative mode does not preserve every Unix metadata feature. Do not treat archive parsing as a security sandbox.";
"guide.safety.title" = "New folders. No silent overwrites.";
"guide.start.body" = "Drop an archive to browse it, or drop files and folders to create a new archive. Use ⌘O to open and ⌘N to create. Double-click folders to explore and files for Quick Look.";
"guide.start.title" = "Start with a file";
"guide.threads.body" = "Thread counts and dictionaries are passed to the native engine. The queue observes a shared thread and estimated-memory budget. Compression methods differ: some operations are inherently serial. Larger dictionaries may need much more RAM and do not always improve compression.";
"guide.threads.title" = "Performance without surprises";
"guide.title" = "A little guidance";
